        "Ahora se define, en Python puro, la función que un endpoint REST invocaría internamente, y se simula una petición `GET /v1/ventas?region=Centro&trimestre=T2`:"
      ],
      "id": "f008ca3a"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "def obtener_ventas(region=None, trimestre=None, departamento=None):\n",
        "    df = data_mart\n",
        "    if region:\n",
        "        df = df[df[\"region\"] == region]\n",
        "    if trimestre:\n",
        "        df = df[df[\"trimestre\"] == trimestre]\n",
        "    if departamento:\n",
        "        df = df[df[\"departamento\"] == departamento]\n",
        "\n",
        "    agregado = (\n",
        "        df.groupby([\"region\", \"trimestre\", \"departamento\"], as_index=False)[\"monto_venta\"]\n",
        "        .sum()\n",
        "        .rename(columns={\"monto_venta\": \"total_ventas\"})\n",
        "    )\n",
        "    return {\"data\": agregado.to_dict(orient=\"records\")}\n",
        "\n",
        "peticion = {\"region\": \"Centro\", \"trimestre\": \"T2\"}\n",
        "respuesta = obtener_ventas(**peticion)\n",
        "respuesta"
